# REGRESSION PIN — indirect-call `&`-param ABI, TYPE axis cell: **40-byte
# non-resource struct** (`struct{5 x int}`), through an ANNOTATED LOCAL
# `Callable`. THE MOST DANGEROUS CELL IN THE TYPE AXIS, and the reason this
# net must run on BOTH backends: at base the two backends disagree on the
# SYMPTOM while sharing the defect.
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the PRE-fix compiler (`git checkout -- src && cargo build`):
#     C    -> rc 0, prints `1` `5` `7` `9`   <-- SILENT WRONG ANSWER, not a crash
#     LLVM -> rc 139 (SIGSEGV)
# POST-fix both backends print `2` `5` `8` `9`.
#
# ⚠ A C-ONLY OR EXIT-CODE-ONLY GATE CALLS THE BASE BEHAVIOUR GREEN. On AAPCS64
# a >16-byte composite travels in a caller-allocated hidden-pointer slot, so
# the by-value/by-pointer mismatch loses the write-through instead of faulting,
# and ASan sees nothing. The exact-stdout assertion is what catches it.
#
# LANE AXIS (self-host driver, `--emit-c` -> cc -> run): rc 0, prints
# `1` `5` `7` `9` — the same SILENT class on the showcase lane. The SH lane's
# own indirect-call ABI defect is filed separately in TODO.md; the direct-call
# control (`bump(&r)`, no `Callable`) prints `2/5/8/9` on the SH lane, which is
# what isolates it to the indirect call.
#
# WHY known_gaps/: zero self-host parity-corpus inflow — `runtime_parity_corpus`
# never descends subdirectories — while the LIVE test still asserts on C + LLVM.
#
# INTENDED: `2` `5` `8` `9`.
struct R:
    int a
    int b
    int c
    int d
    int e

void bump(R &r):
    r.a = r.a + 1
    r.c = r.c + 1

int main():
    Callable[void(R &)] f = bump
    R r = R(1, 5, 7, 9, 11)
    f(&r)
    print(r.a)
    print(r.b)
    print(r.c)
    print(r.d)
    return 0
